  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 20,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Two meters, one bill — read this before trusting a number",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**Agent meter (Loki, `$service`)** — each agent self-reports `cost_usd` on its `api_request` event. Only agents talking *straight to a vendor API* know their price: today that is **claude-code**. `pi` emits `cost_usd=0` for every call because its OpenAI-compatible provider returns no cost in `usage` — so it is **excluded from spend by design** (`| cost_usd != 0`) rather than shown as a misleading $0.00. Its tokens and requests are still counted below. Ralph loops, bebop and OpenClaw emit no `api_request` events, so they never appear on this meter.\n\n**Proxy meter (Prometheus, `litellm_spend_metric_total`, `$model`)** — LiteLLM prices every call that crosses the proxy: `pi`, `bebop`, OpenClaw agents, Compass `gpt-5` / `gpt-5.6-sol`. **This is where pi's real spend lives.** The RTX 3090 models (`$local_models`) also cross it but price at **$0**, so they never show up in a spend panel — that is why the section at the bottom values them separately as *avoided* cost.\n\n**GPU meter (Prometheus, `llamaswap_upstream_*`, since 2026-09-11)** — token counters read from the loaded llama-server itself. It is the only meter that sees callers hitting llama-swap directly, bypassing LiteLLM.\n\nThe agent and proxy meters are disjoint — claude-code does not cross the proxy — so *Total spend* is their sum. Prometheus retains 30d, Loki only 7d: ranges beyond 7d show proxy spend only."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 1,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Spend (range) — agent-reported",
      "description": "Loki meter. Agents with no cost source (pi) are filtered out instead of rendering a false $0.00 — if pi ever starts reporting real cost it appears here automatically.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 5
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "loki",
        "uid": "loki"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "currencyUSD",
          "decimals": 2,
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "area",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ]
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "loki",
            "uid": "loki"
          },
          "queryType": "instant",
          "expr": "sum by (service_name)(sum_over_time({service_name=~\"$service\"} | event_name=`api_request` | cost_usd != `0` | unwrap cost_usd [$__range]))"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Spend (range) — LiteLLM proxy",
      "description": "Prometheus meter. Covers pi, bebop and OpenClaw. The RTX 3090 models cross this meter too but price at $0, so they contribute nothing here — see the local-models section below for what they saved.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 6,
        "y": 5
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "currencyUSD",
          "decimals": 2,
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "area",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ]
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
